+    # h31 -- ONE SHAPE PER PROCESS. Crossing a shape boundary inside a single benchmark
+    # process is the only condition under which this job has ever faulted the card, and it
+    # is isolated by a controlled pair, not inferred: rounds/016/_scratch/meas2/out:23
+    # (one process, --shapes fast,proxy,prod) faults; rounds/016/_scratch/meas3/out:16,33,50
+    # (same binary, same six arms including beat, same cold JIT cache, split per shape) is
+    # rc=0 three times. facts.md:241 ratified "one benchmark process per shape" rounds ago,
+    # but it only ever reached the hand-written meas scripts -- this line still said
+    # ",".join(shapes), which is the direct source of the round 17 and round 18 wedges.
+    #
+    # This removes no out-of-bounds access. It removes the isolated trigger, and it stops
+    # feeding further shapes to an already-sick card (rounds/003/_scratch/gpu2/out:9-18 is
+    # how one fault becomes a wedge). Every ratio the gate computes is within one shape, so
+    # no comparison changes.
+    tmp = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="validation-"))
+    rows = []
+    for s in shapes:
+        out = tmp / f"bench_{s}.json"
